/**
 * Icon set.
 *
 * Every glyph is copied from the upstream renderer rather than redrawn, so markup
 * that reuses upstream class strings also keeps upstream geometry. Upstream ships
 * its icons as a theme-pack registry (`mcode` default = the fill set, `codex` /
 * `rounded` = stroked), keyed by semantic names such as `newChat` / `settings` /
 * `disclosure`; the paths below are the `mcode` pack's, taken verbatim from the
 * extracted bundle. Each icon carries its own viewBox because upstream mixes
 * 20x20, 16x16 and 14x14 frames. Stroke colours always come from the `text-icon_*`
 * token classes at the call site.
 *
 * Most glyphs are filled; `STROKE_ICONS` lists the ones upstream draws as
 * outlines. Which side a glyph belongs on is a property of its upstream ref, not a
 * judgement call — check the ref before moving a name between the two.
 *
 * See `webapp/README.md` ("Re-derive evidence") for the extraction recipe, and the
 * alignment working notes for the name-to-export table.
 */

